## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Câu hỏi hành vi bằng tiếng Anh

**Ba câu, ghi âm liền mạch:**

**"What's your biggest weakness?"**
> *"I go too deep on a problem before asking for help. At my last job I spent nearly two days on an iOS build error that the native developer on my team would have solved in twenty minutes.*
> *What I do now is set a hard rule — one hour without progress and I write down what I've tried, then I ask. Writing it down first helps both sides, and honestly, about half the time I find the answer while writing it.*
> *The last three months I've been working alone with nobody to ask, so I kept the rule by writing into a technical log before searching."*

**"Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone."**

**"Why should we hire you over someone else?"**
> *"I won't claim I'm the strongest React Native developer you'll talk to. What I'd say is this: I shipped something end to end this year, alone, including the parts most people avoid — the native module, the test suite, the pipeline, the store submission.*
> *And I put it in front of real users and watched them get confused, which changed what I built.*
> *So if what you need is someone who finishes things and can tell you honestly where the edges of their knowledge are, that's what I'm bringing."*

